description:
FILED s538a (Opus, 2026-11-13) from the companion one-file run of t/io/argv.t (base 381d9063 -> the s538a tree:
28/23 -> 30/23).  PRE-EXISTING: main 381d9063 answers exactly as the tree on the reproducer.  s538a's #660 (slurp at
EOF is "" once) made io/argv.t's in-place `while (<>)` over an EMPTY second file run its body as perl does, so the
file's own numbering lines up with perl's: rows 13 14 25 26 now pass / run, and the two rows of THIS bug ("STDIN has
something", `is(<>, "ok 11\n")`, perl's 15 16) now show as failing -- on main they were hidden by the off-by-two
numbering.

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3; the s538a worktree's scratch/s538a/pr2/argv3.pl):

    open my $t, '>', "/tmp/x$$" or die; print $t "data\n"; close $t;
    @ARGV = ("/tmp/x$$"); my @all = <>;          # exhaust <>
    open STDIN, "<", "/tmp/x$$" or die; @ARGV = ();
    print eof() ? "1 eof\n" : "1 not eof\n"; my $x = <>; print defined $x ? "2 read $x" : "2 undef\n";
    @ARGV = ("/tmp/x$$"); my @b = <>; print "3 n=", scalar(@b), "\n";
    @ARGV = (); open STDIN, "<", "/tmp/x$$" or die; my $y = <>; print defined $y ? "4 read $y" : "4 undef\n";

  perl:  1 not eof / 2 read data / 3 n=1 / 4 read data
  PCL:   1 eof     / 2 undef     / 3 n=1 / 4 undef

perl's nextargv: when @ARGV is empty and ARGV has not been opened since the last exhaustion (IoFLAGS IOf_START is set
again at the end of a pass, #2684), `<>` / `eof()` open "-" = STDIN.  PCL's <> state (%p-argv-advance,
*p-argv-last-count*, the IOf_START reset of #2684) restarts the FILE sequence when @ARGV is refilled (row 3) but not
the STDIN fallback.  Fix in %p-argv-advance (+ the eof() pseudo-file test, #2703's): at a pass start with @ARGV empty,
read STDIN once per pass.  Rows: io/argv.t 15 16 (blessed by s538a under this task).
